.TH MEETINGINSIGHTS 1 "2026" "meetinginsights 0.6.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
meetinginsights \- record meetings and write minutes, entirely on device
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B meetinginsights
.I command
.RI [ arguments ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Records the microphone and system audio as separate channels, transcribes each
locally with faster-whisper, and writes structured minutes with a local language
model. By default no audio or transcript leaves the machine and no API key is used;
writing the minutes with Claude Code or Gemini CLI is opt-in and sends the transcript
to that service.
.PP
Because the microphone is captured to the left channel and system audio to the
right, "You" comes from audio routing; the voices on the far end are told apart by an
offline diarization model. Action-item owners are read off the transcript labels.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B setup
Prepare the Python environment and download the speech and language models
(about 1.5 GB). Run once, as your normal user. The desktop application offers
to do this for you on first launch, so this is only needed for headless use.
Pass \fB--porcelain\fR to emit machine-readable progress.
.TP
.BI "start " title " [--client " name "] [--focus " text ]
Begin recording. Prints a reminder to tell participants they are being recorded.
\fB--client\fR applies that client's saved glossary; \fB--focus\fR says what matters
in this meeting and adds an "In focus" section to the minutes.
.TP
.B stop " [--capture-only]"
Stop recording, then transcribe and write the minutes. With \fB--capture-only\fR
only the audio is saved; finish later with \fBfinish\fR.
.TP
.BI finish " name"
Transcribe and write the minutes for a recording stopped with \fB--capture-only\fR.
.TP
.B recover " [--list]"
Finish a recording that was cut short and process audio left without minutes.
.TP
.BI "import " file " [title]"
Transcribe an existing audio or video file and write the minutes.
.TP
.B trello " login|logout|status|boards|lists|use|actions|send"
Turn a meeting's action items into Trello cards. \fBlogin\fR reads an API key and a token (from the
terminal or standard input) and stores them privately; \fBuse\fR picks the list; \fBsend\fR
\fIname\fR [\fB--only\fR 1,3] [\fB--dry-run\fR] creates the cards, once per item. Opt-in: nothing
is sent unless you run \fBsend\fR.
.TP
.BI "obsidian " name " [--folder " path "] [--no-transcript]"
Save a meeting as a note, with frontmatter and the transcript, in the Obsidian vault set with
\fBconfig obsidian_vault\fR. Per-client folder, hub and index notes are set with
\fBclient config\fR. Nothing is written outside the vault.
.TP
.BI "search [--client " name "] " words
Find meetings by what was said, in the minutes and the transcripts. Ignores case
and accents; every word must match, and a quoted phrase must match as written.
.TP
.BI "client [list|show|set|rm] " name " [terms]"
Keep a glossary of names and terms for a client.
.TP
.BI "reprocess " name
Transcribe again and rewrite the minutes (\fB--notes-only\fR to skip transcription).
.TP
.BI "rename " name " title"
Rename a meeting.
.TP
.BI "export " name " md|docx|pdf"
Export the minutes and transcript.
.TP
.BI "delete " name
Delete a meeting's minutes, transcript and audio.
.TP
.BI "config [" key " [" value "]]"
Show or set a setting (whisper_model, notes_model, notes_provider, whisper_device, diarize, ...).
.TP
.B status
Report whether a recording is in progress.
.TP
.B ready
Exit 0 if the application is set up, 1 if
.B setup
still needs to be run. Intended for scripts and the desktop app.
.TP
.BI "notes " transcript
Regenerate minutes from an existing transcript file.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B MEETINGINSIGHTS_OUT
Directory for the written minutes. Default ~/MeetingNotes.
.TP
.B MEETINGINSIGHTS_WHISPER_MODEL
faster-whisper model name (small, medium, large-v3-turbo). Default: large-v3-turbo when the GPU libraries are installed, else small.
.TP
.B MEETINGINSIGHTS_LLM_MODEL
Path to a GGUF chat model used for the prose summaries.
.TP
.B MEETINGINSIGHTS_YOU ", " MEETINGINSIGHTS_THEM
Labels for the microphone and system-audio channels.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/MeetingNotes/
Written minutes, one Markdown file per meeting.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/meetinginsights/rec/
Recordings and transcripts.
.SH NOTES
Recording a conversation without informing the other participants is unlawful
in many jurisdictions. Please obtain consent.
.SH SEE ALSO
Project page: https://github.com/bcocheto/meetinginsights-linux
